e_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n    <skill>\n      <name>code-semantic-labeler</name>\n      <description>使用责任链模式实现代码语义标注，将代码中的节点映射到城市业务语义。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/program_snippet/code-semantic-labeler/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>code-splitter-adapter</name>\n      <description>使用适配器模式和工厂模式封装 LangChain 和 LlamaIndex 中的代码切分工具，对外提供统一的调用接口。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/program_snippet/code-splitter-adapter/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>code-to-ast-new</name>\n      <description>将输入的代码转化为 AST（抽象语法树）结构，支持多种编程语言，以 JSON 格式输出 AST 结构。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/program_snippet/code-to-ast-new/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>dataflow-extractor</name>\n      <description>通过静态分析代码片段，提取变量和模块之间的数据流转关系（Dataflow Edges）。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/program_snippet/dataflow-extractor/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>opengrep-compliance</name>\n      <description>Run a hybrid code compliance workflow: local OpenGrep rule scanning first, then LLM analysis for attack chains, concrete fixes, false-positive review, and risk prioritization.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/program_snippet/opengrep-compliance/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"0e196e33-239a-4b82-ada0-86a5a1a44f3c"}],"viewed_images":{},"intent_context":{"intent":"task","original_query":"请把这段视频转换成统一格式，提取关键帧，并截取 00:12 到 00:28 的片段保存下来。","normalized_query":"请把这段视频转换成统一格式，提取关键帧，并截取 00:12 到 00:28 的片段保存下来。","routing_query":"场景：程序片段。场景ID：program_snippet。场景说明：Python、Java、C++ 等程序片段的静态分析、格式校验、AST 解析、代码标准化、语义意图识别、元数据标注、输入输出提取、调用图、数据流、业务流程图、组件文档、示例生成和组件封装场景。需要识别参数：代码内容、编程语言、处理目标。用户原始问题：我将把这段视频转换为统一格式，提取关键帧，并截取00:12到00:28的片段保存下来","scene":"program_snippet","scene_n