data: {"messages":[{"content":"请把这段视频转换成统一格式，提取关键帧，并截取 00:12 到 00:28 的片段保存下来。","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"156fc78b-bdb2-4ac3-a2b3-7d4744e62ab5"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n    <skill>\n      <name>code-semantic-labeler</name>\n      <description>使用责任链模式实现代码语义标注，将代码中的节点映射到城市业务语义。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/program_snippet/code-semantic-labeler/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>code-splitter-adapter</name>\n      <description>使用适配器模式和工厂模式封装 LangChain 和 LlamaIndex 中的代码切分工具，对外提供统一的调用接口。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/program_snippet/code-splitter-adapter/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>code-to-ast-new</name>\n      <description>将输入的代码转化为 AST（抽象语法树）结构，支持多种编程语言，以 JSON 格式输出 AST 结构。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/program_snippet/code-to-ast-new/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>dataflow-extractor</name>\n      <description>通过静态分析代码片段，提取变量和模块之间的数据流转关系（Dataflow Edges）。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/program_snippet/dataflow-extractor/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>opengrep-compliance</name>\n      <description>Run a hybrid code compliance workflow: local OpenGrep rule scanning first, then LLM analysis for attack chains, concrete fixes, false-positive review, and risk prioritization.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/program_snippet/opengrep-compliance/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"0e196e33-239a-4b82-ada0-86a5a1a44f3c"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：场景：程序片段。场景ID：program_snippet\n识别场景：程序片段 (program_snippet)；场景模式：single；候选场景：program_snippet\n任务切分：\n- 请把这段视频转换成统一格式，提取关键帧，并截取 00:12 到 00:28 的片段保存下来。\n任务规划：\n1. 读取输入的原始视频文件，解析其容器协议、编码格式、时长与分辨率等元数据，建立输入样本的基础属性清单与格式兼容性评估表。\n2. 基于程序片段（program_snippet）场景的脚本生成与执行能力，构建自动化处理代码逻辑，明确统一输出格式标准、关键帧抽取的画面差异阈值算法，以及00:12至00:28时间轴切片的精确参数。\n3. 执行媒体处理流水线，完成视频流的解码转码与格式统一，依据算法提取代表性关键帧图像，并按时间戳精准裁剪目标片段，同步记录处理耗时、内存占用及中间校验指标。\n4. 对转换后的视频、关键帧序列及截取片段进行完整性与边界一致性核验，确认时间范围严格对齐00:12-00:28且无丢帧或编码错误后，将标准化产物打包归档并输出可追溯的交付清单。\n场景任务：\n- program_snippet: 我将把这段视频转换为统一格式，提取关键帧，并截取00:12到00:28的片段保存下来。；参数：{'处理目标': '格式转换、关键帧提取、片段截取(00:12到00:28)'}\n已提取参数：{'处理目标': '格式转换、关键帧提取、片段截取(00:12到00:28)'}\n任务提示：\n- 提取必填参数：代码内容。用户提供的函数、类、脚本、源码文件或裸代码片段\n- 提取可选参数：编程语言。代码片段所属语言，如 Python、Java、C++、JavaScript 等\n- 提取可选参数：处理目标。用户希望执行的代码处理任务，如格式校验、AST 解析、标准化、语义意图识别、元数据标注、IO 提取、调用图、数据流、业务流程图、组件文档、示例生成或组件封装\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"a66020d0-5667-4c4e-8b44-f1c7453c885e"},{"content":"我来帮你处理视频。首先让我查找你上传的视频文件。\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":308,"prompt_tokens":11177,"total_tokens":11485,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":239,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":308},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":11177}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-90098664-5bef-9e9c-b851-085359e07159","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f8f60-ea2b-71a3-9140-a615387dcc6e-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"bash","args":{"command":"ls -la /mnt/user-data/uploads/","description":"检查上传目录中的视频文件"},"id":"call_8efb0d5480b84be7bf827b62","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":11177,"output_tokens":308,"total_tokens":11485,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":239}}},{"content":"total 8\ndrwxrwxrwx 2 root root 4096 Jul 23 22:29 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 5 root root 4096 Jul 23 22:29 ..","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"bash","id":"790009ed-fb2b-48ae-9775-6e4abe0afd1e","tool_call_id":"call_8efb0d5480b84be7bf827b62","artifact":null,"status":"success"}],"thread_data":{"workspace_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/7b63db07-089c-4b43-953f-63c9165b2542/user-data/workspace","uploads_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/7b63db07-089c-4b43-953f-63c9165b2542/user-data/uploads","outputs_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/7b63db07-089c-4b43-953f-63c9165b2542/user-data/outputs"},"title":"视频转换与剪辑","artifacts":[],"raw_messages":[{"content":"请把这段视频转换成统一格式，提取关键帧，并截取 00:12 到 00:28 的片段保存下来。","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"156fc78b-bdb2-4ac3-a2b3-7d4744e62ab5"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n    <skill>\n      <name>code-semantic-labeler</name>\n      <description>使用责任链模式实现代码语义标注，将代码中的节点映射到城市业务语义。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/program_snippet/code-semantic-labeler/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>code-splitter-adapter</name>\n      <description>使用适配器模式和工厂模式封装 LangChain 和 LlamaIndex 中的代码切分工具，对外提供统一的调用接口。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/program_snippet/code-splitter-adapter/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>code-to-ast-new</name>\n      <description>将输入的代码转化为 AST（抽象语法树）结构，支持多种编程语言，以 JSON 格式输出 AST 结构。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/program_snippet/code-to-ast-new/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>dataflow-extractor</name>\n      <description>通过静态分析代码片段，提取变量和模块之间的数据流转关系（Dataflow Edges）。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/program_snippet/dataflow-extractor/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>opengrep-compliance</name>\n      <description>Run a hybrid code compliance workflow: local OpenGrep rule scanning first, then LLM analysis for attack chains, concrete fixes, false-positive review, and risk prioritization.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/program_snippet/opengrep-compliance/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"0e196e33-239a-4b82-ada0-86a5a1a44f3c"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：场景：程序片段。场景ID：program_snippet\n识别场景：程序片段 (program_snippet)；场景模式：single；候选场景：program_snippet\n任务切分：\n- 请把这段视频转换成统一格式，提取关键帧，并截取 00:12 到 00:28 的片段保存下来。\n任务规划：\n1. 读取输入的原始视频文件，解析其容器协议、编码格式、时长与分辨率等元数据，建立输入样本的基础属性清单与格式兼容性评估表。\n2. 基于程序片段（program_snippet）场景的脚本生成与执行能力，构建自动化处理代码逻辑，明确统一输出格式标准、关键帧抽取的画面差异阈值算法，以及00:12至00:28时间轴切片的精确参数。\n3. 执行媒体处理流水线，完成视频流的解码转码与格式统一，依据算法提取代表性关键帧图像，并按时间戳精准裁剪目标片段，同步记录处理耗时、内存占用及中间校验指标。\n4. 对转换后的视频、关键帧序列及截取片段进行完整性与边界一致性核验，确认时间范围严格对齐00:12-00:28且无丢帧或编码错误后，将标准化产物打包归档并输出可追溯的交付清单。\n场景任务：\n- program_snippet: 我将把这段视频转换为统一格式，提取关键帧，并截取00:12到00:28的片段保存下来。；参数：{'处理目标': '格式转换、关键帧提取、片段截取(00:12到00:28)'}\n已提取参数：{'处理目标': '格式转换、关键帧提取、片段截取(00:12到00:28)'}\n任务提示：\n- 提取必填参数：代码内容。用户提供的函数、类、脚本、源码文件或裸代码片段\n- 提取可选参数：编程语言。代码片段所属语言，如 Python、Java、C++、JavaScript 等\n- 提取可选参数：处理目标。用户希望执行的代码处理任务，如格式校验、AST 解析、标准化、语义意图识别、元数据标注、IO 提取、调用图、数据流、业务流程图、组件文档、示例生成或组件封装\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"a66020d0-5667-4c4e-8b44-f1c7453c885e"},{"content":"我来帮你处理视频。首先让我查找你上传的视频文件。\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":308,"prompt_tokens":11177,"total_tokens":11485,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":239,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":308},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":11177}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-90098664-5bef-9e9c-b851-085359e07159","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f8f60-ea2b-71a3-9140-a615387dcc6e-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"bash","args":{"command":"ls -la /mnt/user-data/uploads/","description":"检查上传目录中的视频文件"},"id":"call_8efb0d5480b84be7bf827b62","type":"t